hat we've become familiar with issue  statement  money issues statement throw money and  it's fine look the money will be helpful  I'm sure but in this moment this is the  point where the old rulebook gets ripped  up and I think that what people are  looking for is authenticity what people  are looking for is something more raw  something more real something that  reflects a true acknowledgment of the  problem that has been hiding in plain  sight for decades if not centuries and  in awakening not just a statement not  just a cheque but something that proves  that everything is dramatically  different than it was and when we look  around elsewhere look no farther than  what NASCAR did one fell swoop get the  Confederate flag Confederate flag the  hell out of here gone get it out of here  for good the kind of thing that that is  jarring and the kind of thing that  speaks to the awakening that so many  people are having and when I see the  same old formula from the NFL it's like  look hey look at that video was great  even though it didn't match completely  what the players wanted and I think it  would have been better if it would have  been a montage of owners to match the  montage of players if only they had a  employee in the in the league who could  put that oh wait they do that's the guy  who put together the one for the players  and went rogue to do it but but look it  hasn't been perfect but but the  statement was was good and it was Roger  Goodell's finest moment but what you do  after that is what's important and the  old formula of throw money at it and  make a statement and get some good PR  points I don't know that that is the way  to go anymore  no and you know we're gonna talk about a  lot of things they can do and I think  one thing that that would go a long way  that we don't have our list to talk  about is the national anthem if there  are protests the league to support that  back that up you know Jerry Jones has  said repeatedly back that toes on the  line my guys are going to stand for the  national anthem and they have the  Cowboys are one of the only teams that  haven't protested this thing so far but  times have changed this feels different  it's a movement it's a change things are  different now on the league and so they  need to come out  support the players in whatever way they  want a protest and if that's Nealon from  the national anthem and that's Nederland  for the national anthem but there needs  to be around the league solid support  for the players in whatever they want to  do however they want to protest whatever  they want to say they need to use their  platforms as Patrick mahomes pointed out  this week and you're absolutely right  and that's something that Sims and I  talked about earlier in the week that it  can't be the coach who says I support my  guys or the coach who says we're going  to make a team decision look team  decision dilutes the will of the  individual the individual gets overcome  by the team dynamic and the the desires  of the coach of the team leaders end up  trickling down to everyone else even if  that's what they don't want to do what I  have said is every owner and this would  be a perfect opportunity for a montage  of video every owner needs to say not  just it's okay or you know that kind of  passive tolerance that we saw a couple  of years ago it needs to be a clear  affirmative statement that I want every  member of the organization to make a  conscious decision as to what is the  appropriate thing to do during the  national anthem  whether it's kneel sit stand or  something else and I want you to make  that decision and I want you to I  encourage you to make the decision I  encourage you to do the thing that you  feel in your heart you should do and I  support you completely and there will be  no repercussions you will not be cut  because of it you will not be benched  because of it your playing time won't be  limited because of it you won't get a  new contract because of it we support  you and we want you to make this  decision we want you to implement the  decision that is in your heart that's  the kind of clarity because otherwise it  feels reluctant it feels like well yeah  you know we wrote that policy and it's  got a doughnut hole in it that we  probably shouldn't have put in there and  it says should stand instead of must  stand and the lawyers have gotten  involved now and the unions involved so  we got to let we got to let them stand  if they want to stand it can't be that  it's got to be stronger I think you're I  think you're on to something there  absolutely Mike and and you know this  this Jerry Jones needs to talk needs to  come out and we're gonna talk a little  bit more about that later on but the  owners do need to speak out and  their voices need to be loud and they  need to be as one to say we support you  we support you players however you want  to protest whatever you want to do in  this league it is fine by us and there  can't be any repercussions for this  which is what they tried to do a couple  years ago and you know as it turns out I  Colin Kaepernick obviously was right and  everybody should listen a lot sooner  than what they have listened but they're  listening now and I think that's the  point moving forward it's got to be more  and they've got to listen even more to  their players and whatever their players  want they've got to say okay you're  right  we'll let you have it so the official  list of things that the owners can do I  think we can expand to three and things  work better in threes item one make a  clear statement of unconditional support  or whatever any player chooses to do  during the anthem owners need to do it  not coach is not the commissioner no one  else the owners need to do it all 32  need to do it period  hi I'm Mike Tirico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from NBC  Sports

